# Plan ONE collision-free trajectory from start_joints through `waypoints`,
# stopping only on those whose blend_radius is 0 and on the last.
# Planning only — nothing moves, and this planner never touches the arm.
#
# Each leg is planned as PlanToPose / PlanToJoints would plan it, from where
# the leg before it ends, and the legs are overlapped in time, so the arm
# passes a blended waypoint still moving: it cuts the corner and never
# reaches that waypoint exactly. Every overlap keeps the joint velocity and
# acceleration limits and is collision-checked, state by state, against the
# current world; the whole trajectory is then validated like any plan.
Waypoint[] waypoints
# REQUIRED: the configuration the plan starts from (rad, joint_1..7), as on
# PlanToPose.
float64[] start_joints
---
bool success
string message                              # failure explanation when !success
trajectory_msgs/JointTrajectory trajectory  # time-parameterized at full speed
float64 planning_time                       # seconds
# Per waypoint: how far the tool passes from the planned path there, m (0
# where the trajectory stops on it).
float64[] corner_m
# The largest goal_mismatch_rad of the JOINTS waypoints (see PlanToJoints).
float64 goal_mismatch_rad
---
string state
